  <div class="page-card">
    <div class="page-card-header"><div><div class="page-name">E — Hold, Orders List &amp; Detail · User Stories</div></div><span class="badge b-mod1">Module 1</span></div>
    <div class="stories">
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E1 · Hold an order</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to click <strong>Hold</strong> to park this customer's order, so that I can serve someone else at the counter — the cart clears and the held bill is saved with all items intact. The <strong>Held</strong> badge at the top of the cart shows how many bills are on hold.</div><div class="story-demo"><strong>Try it:</strong> Add items → click Hold → cart shows "Cart is empty". Notice the <strong>Held 1</strong> badge at the top right.</div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E2 · Recall a held bill</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to press <kbd>⌥H</kbd> to open the Held Bills list, so that I can see all parked orders — each showing the Bill ID, time, item preview, and total. I click <strong>Recall</strong> to restore it to the cart, or <strong>Delete</strong> to remove it permanently.</div><div class="story-note"><strong>Recall</strong> — restores the held bill back to the cart exactly as it was.<br><strong>Delete</strong> — permanently removes the held bill. Use only if the customer cancelled.</div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E3 · Navigate to the Orders list with ⌥O</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to press <kbd>⌥O</kbd> to open the Orders list, so that I can check statuses, find a specific order, and review what happened today.</div><div class="story-note">There are two separate lists — <strong>Orders</strong> (domestic) and <strong>Export Orders</strong> (international). For Module 1 we only cover the domestic Orders list. Export Orders are covered in <strong>Module 3</strong>.</div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E4 · Read the order list columns</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to understand every column in the Orders list, so that I can instantly see which orders need action without opening each one.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>Tracking code</strong> — unique order reference (e.g. STORE_01-NIBIN-00001). Click it to open the order detail. Give this to the customer if they ask for their order number.<br><br>
        <strong>Created at</strong> — date and time the order was placed.<br><br>
        <strong>Customer</strong> — the account or contact the order is linked to.<br><br>
        <strong>Created by</strong> — the staff member who placed the order.<br><br>
        <strong>Total</strong> — full bill amount including tax.<br><br>
        <strong>Paid</strong> — amount collected so far. ₹0.00 = no payment recorded yet.<br><br>
        <strong>Due</strong> — outstanding balance (Total − Paid). Shown in <span style="color:var(--red);font-weight:700;">red</span> when money is still owed. Goes to ₹0.00 after full payment.<br><br>

        <strong>Dispatch</strong> — tracks whether the warehouse has processed the goods.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>—</strong> — not yet pushed to the warehouse.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <span style="background:var(--amber-light);color:var(--amber);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">+ Push to dispatch</span> — appears when the order needs a manual push. <strong>Click it to send to the warehouse directly from this list.</strong><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <span style="background:var(--amber-light);color:var(--amber);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">In progress</span> — pushed; warehouse is processing.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <span style="background:var(--wisteria-50);color:var(--wisteria-700);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">Dispatched</span> — goods have left the warehouse.<br><br>
        <strong>When does dispatch need a manual push?</strong><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Full payment collected</strong> → dispatch is pushed <em>automatically</em>. No action needed.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Credit sale approved (ship without pay)</strong> → dispatch is pushed <em>automatically</em> once the manager approves.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Partial payment</strong> → dispatch is <em>held</em>. The agent must click <strong>+ Push to dispatch</strong> once the customer pays the remaining balance or the manager approves a credit sale.<br><br>

        <strong>Delivery</strong> — whether goods reached the customer. Shows <span style="background:var(--green-light);color:var(--green);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">Delivered</span> once confirmed; otherwise "—".<br><br>

        <strong>Order</strong> — the document lifecycle of the order. Only 3 possible values:<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <span style="background:var(--amber-light);color:var(--amber);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">Draft</span> — order saved but not yet committed. Payment not collected. Still editable.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <span style="background:var(--green-light);color:var(--green);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">Confirmed</span> — order committed, stock reserved. Reached after payment is collected (or credit sale approved).<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <span style="background:var(--red-light);color:var(--red);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">Voided</span> — order cancelled. No further action possible.<br><br>

        <strong>Order type</strong> — <strong>Domestic</strong> or <strong>Export · [currency]</strong>. Determines which tax rules apply.<br><br>

        <strong>Supply</strong> — GST supply type, derived automatically from the billing address:<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>B2C</strong> — no GSTIN on the billing address → Bill of Supply.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>B2B</strong> — GSTIN present on the billing address → Tax Invoice.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• Blank — Export orders (shown separately in Order type).<br><br>

        <strong>Payment</strong> — the money status, independent from the Order column. 5 possible values:<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Unpaid</strong> — nothing collected yet.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Partial</strong> — some payment received, balance still due.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Paid</strong> — fully collected.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Partial refund</strong> — was fully paid, then part was refunded.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>Refunded</strong> — payment was returned to the customer.<br>
        When Unpaid or Partial, the badge is clickable — tap it to go directly to Add Payment.<br><br>

        <strong>Approvals</strong> — shows any pending request on the order:<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• <strong>+ Request credit</strong> — credit sale requested, waiting for Store Manager sign-off.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• Blank — no pending approval.<br><br>

        <strong>👁 icon</strong> — quick-preview the order summary without leaving the list.<br>
        <strong>⋮ icon</strong> — 3-dot menu for inline actions without opening the order detail.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E4b · Take quick actions directly from the Orders list</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to handle common actions directly on the Orders list without opening the order detail, so that I can serve customers faster at a busy counter.</div><div class="story-note">
        The Orders list is a full action surface — most counter tasks can be done without ever clicking into the order detail:<br><br>
        <strong>Add payment</strong> — click the <strong>Unpaid</strong> or <strong>Partial</strong> badge in the Payment column → opens the payment modal inline.<br>
        <strong>Push to dispatch</strong> — click the <strong>+ Push to dispatch</strong> badge in the Dispatch column → sends to warehouse immediately.<br>
        <strong>Quick preview</strong> — click the <strong>👁</strong> icon → see order summary (customer, total, items) without leaving the list.<br>
        <strong>3-dot menu (⋮)</strong> — per-row actions: View invoice, Reprint, Download, CSV, Send via Email, Send via WhatsApp, Set due date, Request credit sale, Void.<br><br>
        Open the order detail (click tracking code) only when you need full information — History, the What to Do guide, editing the order, or setting addresses.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E5 · Use the status tabs to find orders quickly</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to click the status tabs at the top of the Orders list, so that I can filter to exactly the orders I need without scrolling through everything.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>Important:</strong> The tabs mix different dimensions — some filter by Order status, others by Dispatch status.<br><br>
        <strong>All</strong> — every order regardless of any status.<br>
        <strong>Paid</strong> — orders where status = Confirmed (committed orders).<br>
        <strong>Draft</strong> — orders created but not yet committed. Use this to find orders you still need to collect payment for.<br>
        <strong>Voided</strong> — cancelled orders. Read-only.<br>
        <strong>In progress</strong> — orders pushed to the warehouse but not yet dispatched (dispatch status = ready for dispatch).<br>
        <strong>Dispatched</strong> — orders where goods have left the warehouse (dispatch status = dispatched).<br>
        <strong>Custom</strong> — your own saved filter combination.<br><br>
        <strong>Add filter +</strong> — narrow further by customer name, date range, created by, payment status, etc. Combine multiple filters at once.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E6 · Land on order detail after creating an order</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to land on the order detail page the moment I create an order, so that I can immediately see the tracking code, all order information, and the <strong>What to Do</strong> guide telling me what the next step is — no need to go back to the orders list to find it.</div><div class="story-note">Also reachable from Orders list → click any tracking code.</div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E7 · Read the order summary header</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to read the summary section at the top of the order detail, so that I can confirm all key information is correct before proceeding.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>Tracking code</strong> — unique order reference (e.g. STORE_01-NIBIN-00001). Give this to the customer if they ask for their order number.<br>
        <strong>Created at</strong> — exact date and time the order was placed.<br>
        <strong>Payment</strong> — shows "—" until payment is collected; fills in after payment is added.<br>
        <strong>Customer</strong> — name and phone number linked to this order.<br>
        <strong>Total</strong> — final bill amount including tax.<br>
        <strong>Amount due</strong> — outstanding balance; becomes ₹0 after full payment.<br>
        <strong>Delivery</strong> — the delivery method selected (e.g. Store pickup).<br>
        <strong>Billed By</strong> — the staff member who created the order.<br>
        <strong>Due date</strong> — shows "—" unless a payment deadline is set (see US-E12).<br>
        <strong>Billing address</strong> — the address shown on the invoice.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E8 · Understand the Items and tax breakdown</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to read the Items section of the order detail, so that I can verify each product, quantity, price, HSN code, and tax — and confirm the totals match what I quoted the customer.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>Each line shows:</strong> product name, price, quantity × unit rate, HSN code, tax amount.<br>
        <strong>HSN code</strong> — the commodity code required on GST invoices (e.g. HSN 09083120 for cardamom). The system fills this automatically from the catalog.<br>
        <strong>Items (tag price)</strong> — total before tax.<br>
        <strong>Subtotal (taxable)</strong> — the amount GST is calculated on.<br>
        <strong>Tax (items)</strong> — CGST + SGST combined (B2C domestic) or IGST (inter-state / export).<br>
        <strong>Total</strong> — items + tax.<br>
        <strong>Amount due</strong> — what remains unpaid. Goes to ₹0 once payment is fully collected.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E9 · Read the History section</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to check the History section of the order detail, so that I can see a timestamped record of who created the order and every action taken on it — useful when a customer disputes details or a manager asks who processed an order.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>History is append-only</strong> — each event is logged automatically with the staff name and timestamp. Nobody can delete or edit a history entry.<br><br>
        <strong>Events you will see in History:</strong><br>
        <strong>Created</strong> — order was placed in elPOS.<br>
        <strong>Edited</strong> — order details were modified (items, delivery, address, etc.).<br>
        <strong>Payment added</strong> — a payment was recorded (cash / UPI / card / bank transfer).<br>
        <strong>Refunded</strong> — a payment was reversed.<br>
        <strong>Due date set</strong> — a payment deadline was set or updated on the order.<br>
        <strong>Credit sale accepted</strong> — a Store Manager approved the credit sale request.<br>
        <strong>Voided</strong> — the order was cancelled (direct void or approved void request).<br>
        <strong>Finalized</strong> — the GST invoice was posted to elBooks (automatic, written by the system).<br>
        <strong>Courier changed</strong> — the preferred courier was set or updated.<br>
        <strong>Dispatched</strong> — goods were dispatched, written automatically by elInventory when the warehouse processes the order.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E10 · Follow the "What to Do" step guide</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to read the <strong>What to Do</strong> panel, so that I always know which step I am on in the order lifecycle — and what action I need to take next.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>Counter sale — 3 steps:</strong><br>
        Step 1 · Take the order — Build the cart. (Done when you reach this screen.)<br>
        Step 2 · Collect payment — Add a payment (Cash / Card / UPI) for the order total. The <strong>Collect payment</strong> button takes you directly to the payment screen.<br>
        Step 3 · Confirm &amp; hand over — Confirm the order and hand the goods to the customer.<br><br>
        The active step is highlighted. Complete one step to unlock the next.
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E11 · Send invoice via Email or WhatsApp from order detail</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to tap the 3-dot (⋯) menu on the order detail and choose <strong>Send via Email</strong> or <strong>Send via WhatsApp</strong>, so that I can share the invoice with the customer at any time — even after the order was created without the notify option ticked.</div><div class="story-note"><strong>Send via WhatsApp</strong> → sends the invoice to the customer's registered phone number.<br><strong>Send via Email</strong> → sends to the customer's registered email address.<br>Use this if a customer says they didn't receive their copy, or asks for a resend.</div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E12 · View, print, download, or export the order</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to use the 3-dot (⋯) menu to access document options, so that I can give the customer a copy in whatever format they need.</div><div class="story-note">
        <strong>View invoice</strong> — opens the full invoice preview on screen.<br>
        <strong>Reprint</strong> — sends to the connected receipt printer again (for counter receipts).<br>
        <strong>Download</strong> — saves a PDF copy of the invoice to your device.<br>
        <strong>CSV</strong> — exports the order line items as a spreadsheet (useful for bulk orders the customer wants to reconcile).
      </div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E13 · Set a due date on an order</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to tap the 3-dot (⋯) menu and choose <strong>Set due date</strong>, so that the customer's payment deadline is recorded on the order — and the Due date field shows in red on the Orders list when it passes.</div><div class="story-note">Used for deferred payment arrangements. The due date is visible to both staff and the accounts team. Setting a due date does <em>not</em> automatically grant credit — that requires a credit sale approval (Module 2).</div></div>
      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-E14 · Preview and print the invoice</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to open the invoice preview from the order detail (3-dot → <strong>View invoice</strong>), so that I can verify the itemised bill of supply with HSN codes, CGST/SGST breakdown, and Grand Total before printing or emailing it to the customer.</div></div>
      <div class="story-note" style="margin:0 0 12px;background:var(--purple-light);border-left:3px solid var(--purple);padding:10px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:13px;"><strong>Request credit sale</strong> also appears in the 3-dot (⋯) menu. This is covered in <strong>Module 2 — Credit Sales</strong>.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div><!-- /mod1 -->


