  <div class="section-divider"><span style="font-size:18px;">📤</span><div><div class="sd-title">B — Request Credit Sale (Ship Without Pay)</div><div class="sd-sub">Module 2 · Sales + Store Manager</div></div></div>
  <div class="page-card">
    <div class="page-card-header"><div><div class="page-name">Credit Sales — Approval Flow</div><div class="page-sub">Sales submits → Manager approves → elBooks records it</div></div><span class="badge b-mod2">Module 2</span></div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="col">
        <div class="section-label">What is a Credit Sale?</div>
        <ul class="features">
          <li>Goods are released to the customer <strong>before payment is collected</strong></li>
          <li>Previously called "Ship Without Pay" — same concept, new name</li>
          <li>A Sales staff cannot confirm this alone — it requires <strong>manager approval</strong></li>
          <li>The order sits as <strong>Pending Approval</strong> until the manager acts</li>
          <li>Once approved, a despatch record is created in elInventory as normal</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <div class="section-label">The Approval Flow</div>
        <div class="flow-steps" style="margin-top:8px;">
          <div class="flow-step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Sales submits the order without payment</strong><p>At checkout, chooses "Request credit" → adds reason → submits. Order status: Pending Approval.</p></div></div>
          <div class="flow-step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Manager receives notification</strong><p>Push notification sent. Also visible in <strong>Confirm Approvals</strong> queue.</p></div></div>
          <div class="flow-step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Manager approves in elBooks</strong><p>Reviews the request; Approve → order Confirmed, despatch triggered. Reject → order stays Draft.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-full">
      <div class="stories" style="padding:20px 0 0;">
        <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-B1 · Sales requests a credit sale</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want to submit an order as a credit request instead of collecting payment now, so that goods can be prepared for a trusted customer while payment is arranged — and the request goes to the manager for sign-off.</div><div class="story-note"><strong>Important:</strong> Never submit a credit request without the customer's agreement and the manager's verbal pre-approval. The system enforces approval; this is not a shortcut.</div></div>
        <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-B2 · Store Manager approves a credit request</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Store Manager</strong>, I want to review credit requests in the Confirm Approvals queue and approve or reject each one, so that no goods leave the warehouse on credit without my explicit sign-off — protecting the business from unauthorized credit.</div><div class="story-mgr"><strong>Manager path:</strong> Navigate to <strong>Approvals → Confirm Approvals</strong> → find the pending request → review → Approve or Reject.</div></div>
        <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-B3 · Understand what happens in elBooks</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Store Manager</strong>, I want to know that approved credit orders flow to elBooks as an invoice with the due date set from the customer's payment terms, so that the accounts team can track outstanding balances and send reminders without any manual entry.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
