      <div class="story"><div class="story-id">US-C1 · Due date auto-derived from payment terms</div><div class="story-text">As a <strong>Sales staff</strong>, I want the due date to be set automatically from the customer's elBooks payment terms (e.g. Net 30 → due = confirmed date + 30 days), so that I don't have to calculate or enter it manually — and the accounts team's overdue tracking works correctly.</div><div class="story-note"><strong>What you see:</strong> "Due date" field on the order detail. If the customer has payment terms, it auto-fills on confirmation. If no terms are set, the field stays blank until manually set.</div></div>
